KB-277 D21 probe (permission policy: trailing-* band, recovered denial keeps success).

This step's allow_tools band is exactly ["adapter.copilot.main.tools.s*"] — a
trailing-* band: the first matching pattern wins, so the `shell` policy tool
matches the band and every non-s* policy tool (read in particular) is DENIED.

Make exactly this three-call sequence. Call (2) is ENGINEERED to be denied;
the denial is NOT a step failure — you recover and the step still finalizes
success (a recovered denial keeps the turn's success).

(1) Call the bash tool now, exactly once:

        command: printf d21-shell-band-ok

    This runs: its policy tool name `shell` matches the s* band.

(2) Call the view tool now, exactly once, on the file ../harness_contracts_v1/main.chcl

    This is DENIED (its policy tool name `read` has no matching allow band);
    expect a permission denied result telling you the tool was not allowed.

(3) Call the submit_outcome tool now, exactly once — this step declares no
    payload schema, so the reason lane is the contract:

        outcome = "approved"
        reason  = "D21 recovered denial keeps success: the trailing-* band allowed the shell tool call, the read tool call was denied with a permission event, and the step still finalized approved after recovering"
        comment = "D21 permission band probe"

No other tools, no other calls.